| `test_quality.assertions.consumers.<name>` | string | `{"all": "only", "any": "only", "dict": "only", "frozenset": "only", "list": "only", "max": "only", "min": "only", "next": "first", "set": "only", "sorted": "only", "sum": "only", "tuple": "only"}` in keel and in a generated project; absent, the same map, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.assertions.consumers = {"all": "only", "any": "only", "dict": "only", "frozenset": "only", "list": "only", "max": "only", "min": "only", "next": "first", "set": "only", "sorted": "only", "sum": "only", "tuple": "only"}` | a bare identifier mapped to `only` or `first`; an empty map permits no callee | `tests/assertion_quality.py` (`policy`, `scan`), through the `scripts/config_loader.py` row | Names callees that consume a generator argument: `only` requires a sole argument; `first` uses the first positional argument regardless of further positional arguments. The callee must be a bare name with no binding in the test scope or any nearer enclosing function, including when used in a called nested helper; class bodies are skipped. A custom name may have one module binding, a function definition or import; a second rejects it. Any module binding of a Python builtin name rejects it. Bindings include nested `nonlocal` and `global` writes and `del` targets. The call must have no keywords or `*` or `**` argument unpacking, and synchronous consumers do not credit async generators. A name bound exactly once to a generator in the current or an enclosing function and consumed there counts too. `sum` is `only` because a string start can raise before iteration; both `sum(gen, 0)` and `sum(gen, "")` receive no credit. Invalid policy fails the gate with `SourceTreeError`, preserving the loader's diagnostic lines and naming this key. | attribute calls, argument values, other call shapes or control flow between bindings | always |
